dtsearchpath: the SVR4 manual page path.

With no MANPATH, dtsearchpath used a per-system default and had none for
SVR4, which left the statement without its body. SVR4 keeps its pages in
/usr/share/man, as Sun does.

--- a/programs/dtsearchpath/libCliSrv/UnixEnv.C	2026-11-20 12:03:13
+++ b/programs/dtsearchpath/libCliSrv/UnixEnv.C	2026-11-20 12:03:13
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@
 
     CString temp = getEnvironmentVariable("MANPATH");
     if (temp.isNull())
-#if defined(sun)
+#if defined(sun) || defined(SVR4)
 	manpath = "/usr/share/man";
 #elif defined(_AIX)
 	manpath = "/usr/share/man:/usr/lpp/info";
